{"id":"CVE-2014-3591","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2019-11-29T21:02:23.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T10:50:17.627Z","description":"Libgcrypt before 1.6.3 and GnuPG before 1.4.19 does not implement ciphertext blinding for Elgamal decryption, which allows physically proximate attackers to obtain the server's private key by determining factors using crafted ciphertext and the fluctuations in the electromagnetic field during multiplication.","cwe":["Other"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"GNU","product":"Libgcrypt","versions":["affected before 1.6.3"]},{"vendor":"GNU","product":"GnuPG","versions":["affected before 1.4.19"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.cs.tau.ac.il/~tromer/radioexp/","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnupg-announce/2015q1/000363.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnupg-announce/2015q1/000364.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2015/dsa-3184","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2015/dsa-3185","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2014-3694","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2014-10-29T10:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T10:50:17.985Z","description":"The (1) bundled GnuTLS SSL/TLS plugin and the (2) bundled OpenSSL SSL/TLS plugin in libpurple in Pidgin before 2.10.10 do not properly consider the Basic Constraints extension during verification of X.509 certificates from SSL servers, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof servers and obtain sensitive information via a crafted certificate.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://pidgin.im/news/security/?id=86","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2017:1854","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2017:1854"},{"url":"http://hg.pidgin.im/pidgin/main/rev/2e4475087f04","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-2390-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-2390-1"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2014-11/msg00023.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2014:1376"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/60741","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"60741"},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2014/dsa-3055","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-3055"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2014-11/msg00037.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2014:1397"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/61968","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"61968"}],"vendors":["crypto-libs","openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2014-8155","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2015-08-14T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T13:10:50.869Z","description":"GnuTLS before 2.9.10 does not verify the activation and expiration dates of CA certificates, which allows man-in-the-middle attackers to spoof servers via a certificate issued by a CA certificate that is (1) not yet valid or (2) no longer valid.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/73317","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"73317"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2015-1457.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2015:1457"},{"url":"https://gitlab.com/gnutls/gnutls/commit/897cbce62c0263a498088ac3e465aa5f05f8719c","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://support.f5.com/csp/article/K53330207","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
{"id":"CVE-2014-8564","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2014-11-13T15:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-06T13:18:48.419Z","description":"The _gnutls_ecc_ansi_x963_export function in gnutls_ecc.c in GnuTLS 3.x before 3.1.28, 3.2.x before 3.2.20, and 3.3.x before 3.3.10 allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (out-of-bounds write) via a crafted (1) Elliptic Curve Cryptography (ECC) certificate or (2) certificate signing requests (CSR), related to generating key IDs.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/59991","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"59991"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2014-1846.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2014:1846"},{"url":"http://www.ubuntu.com/usn/USN-2403-1","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-2403-1"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/62294","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"62294"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1161443","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/62284","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"62284"},{"url":"http://lists.opensuse.org/opensuse-updates/2014-11/msg00084.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_SUSE"],"name":"openSUSE-SU-2014:1472"}],"vendors":["crypto-libs"]}
